From ef6b1be0c2313a5bdd7d9e20a695f14320f81d0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev-2f782c1c <dev-2f782c1c@users.noreply.forkmesh.com>
Date: Fri, 26 Jun 2026 20:12:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] perf: stop UI-thread git calls from freezing the agent window
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The StallWatchdog reported repeated multi-second event-loop stalls, all
ultimately blocked in QProcess::waitForFinished() (git) or layout run on
the GUI thread. Fix the worst, most user-visible offenders:

- refreshAgentFilesPanel ran a blocking `git diff --name-only` on *every*
  transcript event, freezing the agent UI in ~1.5-2s bursts while a
  session streamed. The in-memory tool-call files now render instantly and
  the working-tree diff is coalesced (400ms debounce) and run off the
  event loop, so clicking through a streaming agent stays smooth.

- loadWorktreesPanel ran a synchronous `git status` per worktree row,
  which blocked the window for seconds (a 21s stall was reported) on repos
  with many worktrees. Each row now shows a placeholder and fills its
  dirty/clean state in asynchronously; a generation tag drops stale
  callbacks when the table is rebuilt.

Add a small reusable runGitDetached() helper (non-blocking QProcess that
self-deletes and reports on the main thread) backing both fixes.

Also make the StallWatchdog more useful for the remaining stalls: a long
stall is now re-sampled as it drags on (up to 6 distinct spots), so
multi-phase blocks — back-to-back git calls, layout thrash — are
attributed correctly instead of being blamed on whatever the single first
sample happened to catch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
